Z||000000||AkursedX||04-29-2001||10:18 PM||||It seems like I might be possibly joins the ranks of multiple Fierp owners.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>My dad was working on a guy's jeep today and he told him he has a friend selling a 86 coupe for $1000.  70-some thousand miles, auto, 4-banger, gold, I can't remember the rest of the info.  The guy apparently bought it at Carlisle last year, so hopefully it is in good shape.  I am probably going to look at it tomorrow, and I'll take it from there.  I plan on using this Fiero as my winter car and I would be selling my 1994 Plymouth Duster.  I hope I can get 3k for it.  It has 124k miles on it though, but it's totally rust free, undercoated and rust-proofed, the engine has been completely rebuilt by me and my dad, amongst many other things.  I don't know if I should sell a good-running and good shape car for another Fiero, and therein lies my dilemmna.  <P>Although this whole debate is moot if my dad won't borrow me the 1000 bucks to buy the Fiero in 1st place  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  (But i think he will, he has taken a liking to working on my 88GT with me)<P>So does anyone have any opinions?  Should I buy it?  Or keep my Duster?||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||04-29-2001||10:37 PM||||If I were you I would definitely keep the Duster especially since you rebuilt its engine.<P> I owned the 87 coupe you see in my signature below and have since sold it to my brother, which I wish I never, did. It had 67,000 miles on it when I sold it. Since then it has been nothing but trouble for both my brother and me. The head gasket blew because a head bolt broke. The ignition coils go about every six months. Numerous sensors keep crapping out. The ignition module died recently. The water pump went. The alternator went two weeks ago. It always seems to run like crap no matter how well of a tune-up it just had. It’s very very very slow and only gets 21-23 mpg. My formula would get 30 mpg on the highway and 24 in the city with the 2.8-liter engine. It has constant oil leaks. It sounds like a diesel engine when idling. It handles like is on a bowl of jelly and slams over every penny in the road. Everything on the highway can pass him even motor homes pulling a car (just kidding). <P>It's definitely not a reliable car that you should depend on for transportation. My brother has spent so much money on rental cars because the his fiero was broken down that he could have put down a nice down payment on a new car. Maybe it’s just this car or something. Maybe its cursed, but this car is the biggest piece of $hit he has ever owned and he hates it. <P>Don't forget you will be giving up a lot of space going from your duster to the fiero.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-29-2001).]||||reg||1
